{"id":"portswigger-web-security-academy--server-side-vulnerabilities--access-control--user-role-controlled-by-request-parameter","path":"portswigger-web-security-academy/server-side-vulnerabilities/access-control/user-role-controlled-by-request-parameter.md","title":"User role controlled by request parameter","category":"portswigger-web-security-academy","source":"https://github.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/blob/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/portswigger-web-security-academy/server-side-vulnerabilities/access-control/user-role-controlled-by-request-parameter.md","html":"<h1 id=\"user-role-controlled-by-request-parameter\">User role controlled by request parameter</h1>\n<h4 id=\"parameter-based-access-control-methods\"><a href=\"https://portswigger.net/web-security/learning-paths/server-side-vulnerabilities-apprentice/access-control-apprentice/access-control/parameter-based-access-control-methods\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Parameter-based access control methods</a></h4>\n<h2 id=\"description\">Description</h2>\n<p>This lab has an admin panel at <code>/admin</code>, which identifies administrators using a forgeable cookie.</p>\n<p>Solve the lab by accessing the admin panel and using it to delete the user <code>carlos</code>.</p>\n<p>You can log in to your own account using the following credentials: <code>wiener:peter</code></p>\n<h2 id=\"solution\">Solution</h2>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(28)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>as indicated into description, we know the admin panel path, but without admin credentials we can't do nothing, </p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(33)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>so we can do normal login with followring credentials: <code>wiener:peter</code></p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(29)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>analysing the http response after login, we can see that there're into cookie and admin flag set to false and the session ID:</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(30)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>Setting the admin flag to 'true' we can do a vertical privilege escalation</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(32)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>then, go to admin panel and set the flag equals true:</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(37)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(35)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>Now, we can finishing deleting user Carlos:</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(36)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"User role controlled by request parameter screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n","toc":[{"id":"parameter-based-access-control-methods","title":"Parameter-based access control methods","level":4},{"id":"description","title":"Description","level":2},{"id":"solution","title":"Solution","level":2}],"excerpt":"User role controlled by request parameter Parameter-based access control methods Description This lab has an admin panel at /admin, which identifies administrators using a forgeable cookie. Solve the lab by accessing the","searchText":"Parameter-based access control methods Description Solution"}